  "cause": "**The two men who died in Kuwait on Thursday were technicians, and the equipment they were servicing was the equipment meant to see what killed them.** A number of drones entered Kuwaiti airspace on Thursday afternoon; the army says it detected and intercepted them, and that falling shrapnel from the interceptions struck a *\"vital site\"* — an air-defence surveillance station — at about **2 p.m. local time**. Four people were wounded: two Italians, a Kuwaiti and a Pakistani. By evening the two Italians were dead. They worked for **Rheinmetall Italia**, the Italian subsidiary of the German defence group, and were performing maintenance on air-defence systems used by the **Kuwait Armed Forces**; Italian media reported their ages as **36** and **65**, the older man nearing retirement. Rheinmetall said it was *\"in deep mourning\"* and that the two had lost their lives *\"while carrying out their professional duties, as they were providing technical support for air defence systems.\"* **Kuwait** called the attack *\"heinous Iranian aggression\"*; Italy's foreign minister, **Antonio Tajani**, told the Senate that the investigation showed the drone was manufactured in Iran. **Iran denies it.** Foreign Minister **Abbas Araghchi** offered condolences in calls with his Italian and Kuwaiti counterparts, said the incident looked *\"suspicious\"* and like a *\"precooked recipe for war\"*, and offered to work with both governments to *\"determine the cause\"*; the armed-forces spokesman, **Abolfazl Shekarchi**, said Iran had conducted *\"no military or offensive operations.\"* **Ursula von der Leyen** said Europe *\"must step up pressure on Iran to end these unacceptable attacks against its neighbours and our partners in the Gulf.\"* The war is in its **ninth month**: it began in late February when the **US and Israel attacked Iran**, and Iran has since struck Israel and Gulf states hosting American forces. On Thursday, as the deaths were confirmed, **Donald Trump** told troops on Thanksgiving that the US had *\"victory at hand\"* and that the war would end *\"whenever I want it to be, to be honest.\"* In the same week an attack on Saudi Arabia's **Jazan** refinery reportedly killed a Nepalese worker and halted operations, and the Houthis claimed a strike on the kingdom's largest refinery.",
